WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How can men --
You know, again,

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've gone through this
so many times,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:06.873
but how are men most helpful
as allies in a time like this?

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think
it's even more helpful

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:12.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
to realize men's stake in it
You know?

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:16.349
Because, actually, if you look
at the cause of male deaths,

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
speeding and violence, and
you know, you add them all up,

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:23.857
the Women's Movement and the
dissolution of gender role

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:27.293
means that you would have abou
five more years of life to live.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not bad, is it?
-Yeah.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who else can make that offer?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would love that.
Yeah, that would be wonderful.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And also, getting to know
your own children.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, because the system,

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:41.274 size:78% position:39%
as it is, means that,
frequently, men are

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:45.211
estranged from their children,
and men get to be whole people

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
by being active in the hom
and raising

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
or being raised
to raise children

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.552 size:81% position:41%
just like we get to be
whole people by being

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.120 size:88% position:44% line:92%
active outside the home.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've started
a couple magazines.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've helped start
a couple magazines.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel like
there's still a role --

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
because obviously,
it's a very scary time

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
for print journalism --
but for sort of

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:07.000
vibrant journalism to brin
attention to these issues?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you worried at all
about the fact that

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are less platforms
for people --

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:15.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
a young version --
well, less perspective.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:15.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
But somebody starting out
their career now,

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.345 size:88% position:44%
do you feel like there
are enough ways for them

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.246 line:92%
to have the impact that you had?

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, because online, you know
is huge.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
And magazines are still
very important.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what worries me more
is the lack of fact-checking

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-And I think the only way

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna get
really accurate facts

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:35.161 size:88% position:44%
is to pay as we do for
newspapers and magazines

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
at least a little something.
-Right.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:40.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because advertising
is always gonna to, you know

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.835 line:92%
the biggest number of eyeballs

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
which it how we got
the President.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-If there weren't advertising,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
we wouldn't have had that show
that was like

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
watching a roadside accident
-Yeah.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's very --
'Cause the one thing about

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.781
roadside accidents is they don't
show commercials during them

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is very nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.184
You have this -- make this
very interesting observation

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:02.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the book that men have an
issue with women in power

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.290 size:88% position:44%
because it brings them
back to their childhood.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because often,
the last time they saw a woman

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
of authority was school
when they were very young.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think as long as we'r
all raised by women --

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.736 line:92%
women, too -- but women --

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have, of course,
a little self-correction

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we realize
we can do other things.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for men, I think,
really the last time they sa

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
an authoritative woman --
really, an authority

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.749 line:92%
over them -- they were a child

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they feel regressed
when they see it.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, otherwise,
I can't explain why

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:38.525
my grown-up male journalis
friends say things like,

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.361
"I cross my legs
whenever I see Hillary Clinton."

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is that about?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.499
You know, "She reminds me
of my wife outside --"

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:50.036
I mean, you know, intelligen
men say these crazy things

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:53.039 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah. Maybe we're just
not that intelligent.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, no.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:58.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I'm not going there.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you -- Seeing this field
of candidates --

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.482 size:88% position:44%
Obviously, it's a very
diverse field right now.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:03.416 line:92%
There's a lot of candidates.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:06.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you optimistic,
moving forward?

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you feel?
-Yeah, I am opt--

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is the most diverse field
of candidates,

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my position is,
I would work my heart out

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
for any one of them.
-Yeah.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.297 line:92%
-It's character that matters

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:20.667
and they all have so much
better character than --

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.902 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:27.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:32.045
But I do think that
we have a problem of looking up.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we have
a case of the "shoulds" --

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:35.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What should I do?"
-Yeah.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.284 size:78% position:39%
-And then we don't --
We become uncertain,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when we look at each other
we know what to do.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
Well, I hope we all

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
do the right thing
when the time comes.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you so much
for being here.

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's such an honor to have you
-No, thank you.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.095 line:92%
-Gloria Steinem, everybody

